    "abstract": "Parts figure for the trim air pressure regulating valve installation, covering the regulator, the manifold, the filter, the ducting and the transmitter, with the diaphragm and torque motor regulators shown as alternates.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the trim air pressure regulating valve and the manifold items around it at all four zone positions.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows one valve position; the four positions are identical apart from duct length. Item 10 and item 10A are alternates and are not interchangeable in either direction: item 10 is the torque motor regulator with position feedback and item 10A is the earlier diaphragm unit with a pneumatic reference. Ordering across the pair produces a valve the zone controller cannot read, so the effectivity and not the nomenclature governs. The connector boss at item 20 exists on the manifold only in the post-modification standard. Duct item 40 is 40 mm shorter in the post-modification standard."
    },
